From: oveRTOS
Subject: [PATCH] tcg/tci: call the TB lookup helper directly on Emscripten

TCI calls the helpers of TCG call ops through libffi. On Emscripten,
ffi_call() calls into JavaScript (ffi_call_js), which converts each
BigInt argument and calls back through the function table and
Asyncify's export wrappers. In a browser profile mid shell loop, the
helpers under ffi_call() accounted for only about a fifth of its
samples; the rest was this glue.
helper_lookup_tb_ptr() ends every indirect branch and, with M-profile's
1 KiB target pages, many direct ones, so it is most helper calls. Call
it directly and leave its result in stack[0], where ffi_call() puts it.
The interpreter loop and the helper are already outside Asyncify, and a
longjmp out of the helper unwinds like the softmmu helpers that the
interpreter already calls directly.

On the FreeRTOS AN500 Linux bundle in headless Chromium, against the
same recipe without this patch and identical firmware, ffi_call() fell
from 50% to 16% of the vCPU thread in a profiling build mid shell loop,
and no TB lookup went through libffi (6.8% of samples before). A
3,000-step shell loop took 7.5-7.7 s instead of 12.3-14.9 s over five
interleaved rounds. lvbench averaged 13 FPS instead of 8-9 over two
rounds, with render time falling from 57 to 35-36 ms per redraw.

---
--- a/tcg/tci.c
+++ b/tcg/tci.c
@@ -24,6 +24,9 @@
 #include "disas/dis-asm.h"
 #include "tcg-has.h"
 #include <ffi.h>
+#ifdef EMSCRIPTEN
+#include "exec/helper-proto-common.h"
+#endif
 
 
 /*
@@ -363,7 +366,20 @@
 
                 /* Helper functions may need to access the "return address" */
                 tci_tb_ptr = (uintptr_t)tb_ptr;
+#ifdef EMSCRIPTEN
+                /*
+                 * libffi calls through JavaScript here.  Call the TB lookup
+                 * directly and leave its result where ffi_call() does.
+                 */
+                if (func == (void *)helper_lookup_tb_ptr) {
+                    stack[0] = (uintptr_t)helper_lookup_tb_ptr(
+                        (CPUArchState *)(uintptr_t)stack[0]);
+                } else {
+                    ffi_call(cif, func, stack, call_slots);
+                }
+#else
                 ffi_call(cif, func, stack, call_slots);
+#endif
             }
 
             switch (len) {
